/Title (Recovery first compares supported cash-yield and direct-fee assumptions. The shared-buffer statistic does not inject extra money. A finite grid then considers permitted date delays, discretionary trims, goal scope and savings step-ups. Lifestyle locks, date locks and hard goals restrict eligible changes. Candidates are ranked deterministically, up to a shortlist are re-simulated, and Pareto filtering retains non-dominated tested options across money, delay and effort. An additional-income search estimates a deterministic lower bound; it is not a salary guarantee.)
